{"user_request": "Please post a concise comment on archive-index document `doc_archive_feb2023_churn` that points reviewers to the original main working document for the February 2023 mid-segment churn investigation. Identify the document, its owner and intended document status, and the analytical sections it was initially set up to hold. Keep this as an archival pointer rather than reconstructing the investigation’s findings.", "today": "2028-01-01", "tool": "post_doc_comment", "arguments": {"doc_id": "doc_archive_feb2023_churn", "body": "Original working document: “Mid-seg churn spike -- Feb 2023 investigation” (owner: Riley). It began as a skeleton and was intended to remain a living investigation document. Its initial sections were the signal writeup, baselines, hypothesis list, and cohort cuts. This is an archival pointer, not a restatement of findings."}, "checks": [{"check_id": "riley_138_02", "path": "args", "criterion": "The comment clearly identifies the original main working document as titled “Mid-seg churn spike -- Feb 2023 investigation,” rather than presenting the later institutional writeup as the original working document.

The comment states that Riley owned the working document and that it was intended to remain a living document updated throughout the investigation.

The comment says the document was initially designed to hold the signal writeup, baselines, hypothesis list, and cohort cuts. It remains a concise archival pointer and does not reconstruct the investigation’s findings.", "value": {"doc_id": "doc_archive_feb2023_churn", "body": "Original working document: “Mid-seg churn spike -- Feb 2023 investigation” (owner: Riley). It began as a skeleton and was intended to remain a living investigation document. Its initial sections were the signal writeup, baselines, hypothesis list, and cohort cuts. This is an archival pointer, not a restatement of findings."}}]}
